summary:
Rescaling MLM-Head for Neural Sparse Retrieval
@yjoonjang et al. find that pretrained encoders with large MLM-head scales face degradation in sparse retrieval, and introduce a zero-cost rescaling correction to stabilize training.
📝

Multi-Vector Embeddings are Provably More Expressive than Single Vector Embeddings
@Raj_Jayaram_ proves that approximating multi-vector similarity with single vectors requires exponentially more dimensions.
📝

CAMI: Cost-Aware Agent-Guided Multi-Indexing for Semantic Retrieval
@adnanqidw_ai et al. at IBM present a framework that treats multi-index construction as a budgeted, multi-objective portfolio selection problem.
📝

As It Was: Aligning LLM Search Evaluation with Historical User Preferences
@AliVardasbi et al. at Spotify ground LLM search judges with historical interaction summaries per result, improving alignment with user preferences on ambiguous queries.
📝

Can Language Models Actually Retrieve In-Context? Drowning in Documents at Million Token Scale
@darvog1 et al. show that LLMs can retrieve from million-token corpora but collapse from attention dilution, and propose length-aware fixes.
📝

IntentTune: Using user demand and personalization to resolve "unknown" query intents for e-commerce search
@RachithAiyappa et al. at eBay resolve ambiguous e-commerce queries by combining demand signals with personalized search history.
📝

Autonomous Information Seeking: A Roadmap for Agentic Recommender Systems
@xylinhaha et al survey agentic recommenders, presenting a taxonomy based on autonomy &amp; 3 paradigms: agent-assisted recommendation, agent-as-recommender, agent-as-user-simulator
📝

Quantifying and Expanding the Theoretical Capacity of Late-Interaction Retrieval Models
@Julian_a42f9a et al. prove MaxSim exactly replicates non-negative inner products and extend it for exact real-valued products, improving negation queries.
📝

Multilingual Semantic Retrieval for Apple Music Search
@vishalaksh23 et al. at Apple present a multilingual bi-encoder for music search that boosts recall on misspelled and cross-lingual queries, lifting conversion rate by 2.28%.
📝
